Wire Representation Use it for <code>wire="text"</code> (default) String prompt atoms Plain completion programs and text-only judge-server workflows <code>wire="tokens"</code> Exact token-ID tuples Autonomous tools and chat boundaries that must survive without decode/re-encode changes <p>For chat prompts, call <code>runtime.chat_prefix(messages, role="main", ...)</code> and pass the result to <code>lit</code> inside your program. Rendering uses the selected engine's chat template. Model-specific boundaries, including Harmony token sequences, remain engine-owned.</p> <pre><code>messages = [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain why the sky is blue."}]
prefix = runtime.chat_prefix(messages)

def program():
    return force(out_text(infer(lit(prefix), max_tokens=128)))
</code></pre> <p>The snippet assumes the corresponding DSL imports and an active runtime. The autonomous tool loop handles conversation rendering for you.</p>
